Limitations:

- Collocated SIMPLE without Rhie-Chow interpolation: an odd-even pressure mode grows on the residual plateau (amplitude reported per run as pressure_odd_even_amplitude). The pair-averaged estimator is immune to it; the legacy two-column estimate is not (reported as pressure_gradient_two_station_legacy).
- Outer u/p gates 2e-5 / 5e-4 (the case's documented residual plateau); continuity and mass flow are converged to 1e-6.
- P12-DIFF-002-UC-001: the pair-averaged dp/dx carries a residual bias against the derived discrete-exact value of 9.93e-04 (64x8), 1.06e-04 (96x12), 2.13e-07 (144x18), tracking the odd-even amplitude. On 64x8 that is 8.3e-04 relative, so the discrete-exact gradient checks there pass with only 1.2x margin on their (unchanged) 1e-3 bound, and the dp/dx asymptotic-order study starts at 96x12 instead.
- P12-DIFF-002-UC-001: the centreline sampling error constant is 3x larger for even ny than for odd, so its grid triplet must be parity-consistent (64x8 / 96x12 / 144x18 here); 216x27 is used only for the pressure gradient.
- Runtimes are wall-clock and not deterministic.

